    authors:
      - given-names: Patrick
        family-names: Zippenfenig
    year: 2023
    publisher:
      name: Zenodo
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7970649
    url: "https://open-meteo.com/"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/open-meteo/open-meteo"
    notes: "Citation form requested by Open-Meteo. API data are licensed CC BY 4.0; the Open-Meteo source code is AGPLv3 or any later version; commercial API use is governed by https://open-meteo.com/en/terms. Source of Open-Meteo ERA5 and forecast products used by this software. The retained historical GFS rule15 case is retrieved separately from NOAA public S3, as cited below."
  - type: data
    title: "NOAA Global Forecast System (GFS), 0.25 degree operational forecast archive"
    authors:
      - name: "NOAA National Weather Service, National Centers for Environmental Prediction"
    url: "https://registry.opendata.aws/noaa-gfs-bdp-pds/"
    license-url: "https://www.weather.gov/disclaimer"
    notes: "The retained historical rule15 case uses the 2023-06-30 00 UTC GFS cycle obtained directly from NOAA public S3, not Open-Meteo. GeoAI extracted the containing grid cell and averaged eight 3-hourly instantaneous temperature samples per UTC day. These are modified research inputs, not an official NOAA/NWS product or endorsement; NOAA/NWS material retains its public-domain status under the linked usage conditions."
